<title>USA: Tappan Zee Financial Inc Q2 net lower.</title>
<headline>Tappan Zee Financial Inc Q2 net lower.</headline>
<dateline>TARRYTOWN, N.Y. 1996-10-30</dateline>
<text>
<p>TAPPAN ZEE FINANCIAL, INC. AND SUBSIDIARY</p>
<p>			   (Unaudited)</p>
<p>			(In thousands, except per share data)</p>
<p>				 Three Months Ended  Six Months Ended</p>
<p>					   September 30,  September 30,</p>
<p>					   1996    1995   1996     1995</p>
<p> Total interest income	    2,155   1,823  4,243    3,590</p>
<p> Total interest expense	   1,018   1,040  2,022    1,979</p>
<p> Net interest income		1,137     783  2,221    1,611</p>
<p> Provision for loan losses	   20	25     26	 55</p>
<p>Net interest income after</p>
<p>  provision for loan losses     1,117     758  2,195    1,556</p>
<p> Non-interest income		   34	31     74	 64</p>
<p> Total non-interest expense     1,306     513  1,983	993</p>
<p>(Loss) income before</p>
<p>  income taxes			(155)     276    286	627</p>
<p> Income tax (benefit) expense   (229)     110   (42)	260</p>
<p> Net income				74     166    328	367</p>
<p> Earnings per share		  0.05	--   0.23	 --</p>
<p>SOURCE  Tappan Zee Financial, Inc.</p>
<p>NOTE: The company said results for the three and six month period ending September 30 1996 included a non-recurring charge of $538,000 ($329,000 net of taxes) for a special assessment.</p>
<p>Net income for the same period was impacted by a tax benefit of $166,000 due to a recently enacted change in New York State tax law.</p>
<p>-- New York Newsdesk 212 859-1610</p>
